1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,299
A glass stovetop looks beautiful until
it's covered

2
00:00:03,309 --> 00:00:06,535
in burnt-on spills and cloudy streaks.

3
00:00:06,896 --> 00:00:10,645
And one wrong scrub can leave scratches
forever.

4
00:00:11,795 --> 00:00:14,107
Here are seven safe steps to bring your

5
00:00:14,117 --> 00:00:18,284
glass cooktop back to a mirror shine
without damaging it.

6
00:00:19,435 --> 00:00:22,569
No special skills are needed, just
patience.

7
00:00:22,929 --> 00:00:26,249
We also cover what to do with the toughest
stains.

8
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:27,963
WikiTube.

9
00:00:28,196 --> 00:00:30,448
Whatever it is, here's how.

10
00:00:30,733 --> 00:00:34,136
Glass-ceramic cooktops are tougher than
they look, but

11
00:00:34,146 --> 00:00:35,307
they can scratch.

12
00:00:35,760 --> 00:00:39,698
The golden rule is simple: soften first,
and

13
00:00:39,708 --> 00:00:41,588
scrape only when you must.

14
00:00:42,552 --> 00:00:45,155
Heat bakes spills onto the glass, so the

15
00:00:45,165 --> 00:00:47,418
cleaning is about loosening them with a
gentle

16
00:00:47,428 --> 00:00:50,841
product and some time, then lifting them
off.

17
00:00:51,504 --> 00:00:54,686
We'll use baking soda, a little vinegar, a

18
00:00:54,696 --> 00:00:57,763
cooktop cleaner, and a razor scraper for
the

19
00:00:57,773 --> 00:00:59,433
really stubborn spots.

20
00:00:59,979 --> 00:01:02,883
Always check your manual for any special
instructions

21
00:01:02,893 --> 00:01:03,926
from the maker.

22
00:01:04,286 --> 00:01:06,584
The whole job takes about half an hour,

23
00:01:06,643 --> 00:01:08,386
and most of that is waiting for the

24
00:01:08,396 --> 00:01:09,707
cleaner to work.

25
00:01:10,267 --> 00:01:11,392
Here's what you need.

26
00:01:11,753 --> 00:01:13,865
Baking soda and white vinegar.

27
00:01:14,156 --> 00:01:17,754
A cooktop cleaner cream, made for glass or
ceramic.

28
00:01:18,045 --> 00:01:20,590
A flat razor scraper, which is sold for

29
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:24,407
cooktops, and a couple of clean microfiber
cloths.

30
00:01:24,953 --> 00:01:26,404
And a damp towel.

31
00:01:26,950 --> 00:01:30,946
Don't use steel wool, scouring pads,
bleach or

32
00:01:30,956 --> 00:01:34,960
abrasive powders, because they can scratch
or stain the glass.

33
00:01:35,414 --> 00:01:39,117
Everything here is inexpensive and easy to
find.

34
00:01:39,667 --> 00:01:40,606
Step one.

35
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:43,732
Make sure all burners are off, and wait

36
00:01:43,742 --> 00:01:46,388
until the stovetop is completely cool.

37
00:01:47,353 --> 00:01:49,990
Many cooktops have a hot-surface light
that stays

38
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,402
on until the glass is safe to touch.

39
00:01:52,856 --> 00:01:55,203
Cleaning a hot surface can burn you, and

40
00:01:55,213 --> 00:01:58,372
cold cleaner on hot glass can leave
streaks,

41
00:01:58,382 --> 00:02:01,493
or even crack the surface in extreme
cases.

42
00:02:02,643 --> 00:02:07,077
Take any pans, pot holders and utensils
off the top.

43
00:02:08,227 --> 00:02:10,063
This is also a good time to open

44
00:02:10,073 --> 00:02:12,429
a window and tie back long hair.

45
00:02:12,790 --> 00:02:15,450
Never rush this stage, because a few extra

46
00:02:15,460 --> 00:02:17,911
minutes of waiting makes the whole job
much

47
00:02:17,921 --> 00:02:19,755
safer and easier.

48
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:21,379
Step two.

49
00:02:21,926 --> 00:02:24,992
Start with a dry or slightly damp
microfiber

50
00:02:25,002 --> 00:02:29,091
cloth, and wipe away crumbs, dust and any
loose

51
00:02:29,101 --> 00:02:29,727
food.

52
00:02:30,273 --> 00:02:33,189
Don't push the debris around with
pressure, because

53
00:02:33,199 --> 00:02:36,658
a hard crumb dragged across the glass can
scratch it.

54
00:02:37,460 --> 00:02:40,153
Lift it, or sweep it into your hand.

55
00:02:41,303 --> 00:02:44,346
Removing this loose layer first means your
cleaner

56
00:02:44,356 --> 00:02:46,503
can focus on the stuck-on stains.

57
00:02:46,957 --> 00:02:49,582
Check around the edges and the burner
rings,

58
00:02:49,592 --> 00:02:51,391
where food tends to hide.

59
00:02:51,844 --> 00:02:54,540
If your stove has a control lock, activate

60
00:02:54,550 --> 00:02:56,827
it, so nobody switches on a burner by

61
00:02:56,837 --> 00:02:58,763
accident while you clean.

62
00:02:59,300 --> 00:03:00,379
Step three.

63
00:03:00,670 --> 00:03:03,342
Sprinkle a generous layer of baking soda
over

64
00:03:03,352 --> 00:03:06,001
the dirty areas, then spray it with white

65
00:03:06,011 --> 00:03:09,414
vinegar, or hot water, until it fizzes and

66
00:03:09,424 --> 00:03:11,037
forms a loose paste.

67
00:03:11,839 --> 00:03:14,789
Baking soda is a very mild abrasive, so

68
00:03:14,799 --> 00:03:17,480
it won't hurt the glass, while the fizzing

69
00:03:17,539 --> 00:03:19,164
helps loosen residue.

70
00:03:20,128 --> 00:03:23,067
Soak a clean towel in hot water, wring

71
00:03:23,077 --> 00:03:25,468
it out and lay it over the area

72
00:03:25,492 --> 00:03:27,790
for fifteen to twenty minutes.

73
00:03:28,592 --> 00:03:31,856
The warm moisture softens burnt-on food,
so you

74
00:03:31,866 --> 00:03:33,386
won't need force later.

75
00:03:33,747 --> 00:03:36,198
If the towel cools down, replace it with

76
00:03:36,208 --> 00:03:37,484
a fresh hot one.

77
00:03:38,031 --> 00:03:40,944
The longer the stain stays damp and warm,

78
00:03:41,003 --> 00:03:43,057
the easier it comes off.

79
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:44,598
Step four.

80
00:03:45,145 --> 00:03:48,037
Remove the towel and use a microfiber
cloth

81
00:03:48,047 --> 00:03:50,220
or a soft sponge to wipe the paste

82
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:52,098
away in gentle circles.

83
00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:55,526
Rinse your cloth often in warm water so

84
00:03:55,536 --> 00:03:57,265
you don't spread dirt around.

85
00:03:58,067 --> 00:04:00,680
For general grime, you will see the
residue

86
00:04:00,690 --> 00:04:02,141
lifting easily now.

87
00:04:02,594 --> 00:04:04,976
Wipe the whole surface down with a clean

88
00:04:04,986 --> 00:04:07,946
damp cloth to remove all the baking soda.

89
00:04:08,399 --> 00:04:10,944
If any burnt patches remain, move on to

90
00:04:10,954 --> 00:04:13,681
the next step instead of scrubbing harder.

91
00:04:14,646 --> 00:04:16,793
Resist the urge to press hard.

92
00:04:17,153 --> 00:04:19,674
If a spot refuses to move, the right

93
00:04:19,684 --> 00:04:23,085
answer is more time, not more force.

94
00:04:23,633 --> 00:04:24,689
Step five.

95
00:04:25,050 --> 00:04:27,873
For burnt-on spots, apply a few drops of

96
00:04:27,883 --> 00:04:30,496
cooktop cleaner to the spot, and let it

97
00:04:30,506 --> 00:04:32,131
sit for a few minutes.

98
00:04:32,584 --> 00:04:35,172
Hold a razor scraper at a shallow angle,

99
00:04:35,266 --> 00:04:38,461
about thirty to forty-five degrees, and
push it

100
00:04:38,471 --> 00:04:42,359
gently across the spot with light, even
pressure,

101
00:04:42,488 --> 00:04:45,366
always keeping the blade flat on the
glass.

102
00:04:45,913 --> 00:04:48,910
Never scrape with the corner, and never
use

103
00:04:48,920 --> 00:04:51,032
a worn or damaged blade.

104
00:04:51,579 --> 00:04:53,668
Wipe off the residue as you go.

105
00:04:54,214 --> 00:04:57,568
Wear a glove, and keep your fingers behind
the blade.

106
00:04:58,022 --> 00:05:00,462
Always check that the scraper is designed
for

107
00:05:00,472 --> 00:05:03,457
glass cooktops, and replace the blade when
it

108
00:05:03,467 --> 00:05:05,254
gets dull or chipped.

109
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:06,856
Step six.

110
00:05:07,310 --> 00:05:09,575
Now put a small amount of cooktop cleaner

111
00:05:09,585 --> 00:05:11,956
cream on the glass, and rub it over

112
00:05:11,966 --> 00:05:15,517
the whole surface with a clean cloth or
paper towel.

113
00:05:16,180 --> 00:05:19,467
This cream cleans lightly, removes the
film left

114
00:05:19,477 --> 00:05:22,971
by earlier cleaning, and leaves a
protective layer.

115
00:05:23,773 --> 00:05:25,713
Let it dry to a light haze if

116
00:05:25,723 --> 00:05:28,326
the directions say so, and then buff it

117
00:05:28,336 --> 00:05:32,978
off with a dry microfiber cloth, using
circular motions.

118
00:05:33,432 --> 00:05:36,276
You should see a clear, streak-free shine.

119
00:05:36,637 --> 00:05:38,447
A thin coat is enough.

120
00:05:39,411 --> 00:05:41,956
Polish in the direction of the light, and

121
00:05:41,966 --> 00:05:44,345
you will spot any streaks instantly.

122
00:05:45,147 --> 00:05:47,700
A dry cloth finishes the job.

123
00:05:48,233 --> 00:05:49,428
Step seven.

124
00:05:49,975 --> 00:05:53,085
A few habits will make future cleaning
faster.

125
00:05:54,236 --> 00:05:57,218
Wipe up spills as soon as the surface is
cool.

126
00:05:58,369 --> 00:06:01,563
Take extra care with sugary spills, which
can

127
00:06:01,573 --> 00:06:03,955
pit the glass if left to harden, and

128
00:06:03,965 --> 00:06:06,251
follow the manufacturer's advice.

129
00:06:06,612 --> 00:06:10,256
Use flat-bottomed cookware that matches
the burner size,

130
00:06:10,548 --> 00:06:13,452
lift pans instead of sliding them, and
check

131
00:06:13,462 --> 00:06:16,177
that the bottom is clean and dry before
use.

132
00:06:16,631 --> 00:06:19,405
Give your stovetop a quick wipe after
cooking,

133
00:06:19,638 --> 00:06:21,901
and a full cleaning once a week.

134
00:06:22,703 --> 00:06:25,828
Following these habits, your weekly
cleaning will take

135
00:06:25,838 --> 00:06:27,311
only five minutes.

136
00:06:27,603 --> 00:06:31,015
Easy, and your glass will last for years.

137
00:06:31,567 --> 00:06:33,821
If a spot survives the paste and the

138
00:06:33,831 --> 00:06:36,662
scraper, do not scrub harder.

139
00:06:37,627 --> 00:06:41,146
Melted sugar and plastic are special
cases, because

140
00:06:41,156 --> 00:06:43,350
they can pit the glass as they cool.

141
00:06:44,314 --> 00:06:47,149
Many manufacturers say to scrape them off
while

142
00:06:47,159 --> 00:06:50,896
the surface is still warm, so check your
manual first.

143
00:06:51,443 --> 00:06:54,147
A white or rainbow haze that wipes clean

144
00:06:54,322 --> 00:06:58,466
is usually mineral film, and cooktop cream
removes it.

145
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:01,879
Cleaning cannot fix damaged glass.

146
00:07:02,332 --> 00:07:04,621
If you see a crack, even a hairline

147
00:07:04,631 --> 00:07:07,057
one, stop using the cooktop.

148
00:07:07,417 --> 00:07:11,065
Spills can reach the electrical parts
underneath, and

149
00:07:11,075 --> 00:07:13,616
the glass can break further when it heats
up.

150
00:07:14,766 --> 00:07:16,986
Switch it off at the circuit breaker and

151
00:07:16,996 --> 00:07:18,841
call an appliance technician.

152
00:07:19,991 --> 00:07:22,860
Deep scratches cannot be buffed out, but
they

153
00:07:22,870 --> 00:07:24,994
are usually only cosmetic.

154
00:07:26,144 --> 00:07:28,433
Have the technician check the unit before
you

155
00:07:28,443 --> 00:07:29,568
use it again.

156
00:07:30,133 --> 00:07:33,151
Most scratches come from things under the
pans,

157
00:07:33,210 --> 00:07:34,440
not from cleaning.

158
00:07:34,673 --> 00:07:38,076
Grains of salt, sugar or rice trapped
beneath

159
00:07:38,086 --> 00:07:41,010
a pot grind into the glass when it moves.

160
00:07:42,161 --> 00:07:45,306
Wipe the bottom of each pan before it goes
on.

161
00:07:46,456 --> 00:07:49,059
Do not use the cooktop as extra counter

162
00:07:49,069 --> 00:07:52,008
space, and do not drop cans or heavy

163
00:07:52,018 --> 00:07:52,969
lids on it.

164
00:07:54,119 --> 00:07:57,638
Rough cast iron bottoms scratch easily, so
lift

165
00:07:57,648 --> 00:07:59,540
them instead of dragging them.

166
00:08:00,100 --> 00:08:03,849
Here are the three mistakes that scratch
glass stovetops.

167
00:08:04,651 --> 00:08:09,375
First, using abrasive pads, steel wool or
gritty powders.

168
00:08:10,038 --> 00:08:11,837
They leave permanent marks.

169
00:08:12,383 --> 00:08:15,752
Second, cleaning while the surface is hot,
which

170
00:08:15,762 --> 00:08:18,048
can burn you and leave streaks.

171
00:08:18,595 --> 00:08:21,116
And third, scraping with the corner of the

172
00:08:21,126 --> 00:08:23,191
blade or at a steep angle.

173
00:08:23,854 --> 00:08:26,746
Keep the blade flat and shallow, use light

174
00:08:26,756 --> 00:08:30,250
pressure, and let the cleaner and time do
the work.

175
00:08:31,052 --> 00:08:33,269
When in doubt, check your manual.

176
00:08:33,815 --> 00:08:36,301
If you are ever unsure, test any new

177
00:08:36,311 --> 00:08:38,656
product on a small corner first.

178
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:40,290
Let's recap.

179
00:08:40,581 --> 00:08:42,473
Switch off and let it cool.

180
00:08:43,275 --> 00:08:44,980
Wipe off loose debris.

181
00:08:45,527 --> 00:08:47,862
Make a baking soda paste and warm it

182
00:08:47,872 --> 00:08:49,114
with a damp towel.

183
00:08:49,474 --> 00:08:50,611
Wipe it clean.

184
00:08:51,762 --> 00:08:55,209
Scrape stubborn spots safely with a flat
blade.

185
00:08:56,173 --> 00:08:58,227
Polish with cooktop cleaner.

186
00:08:58,681 --> 00:09:01,687
And build the habits that prevent burnt-on
messes.

187
00:09:02,838 --> 00:09:07,504
Seven steps, about thirty minutes, and a
stovetop that gleams.

188
00:09:08,654 --> 00:09:11,836
For stubborn stains, take extra care, and
a

189
00:09:11,846 --> 00:09:14,365
cracked cooktop needs a technician.

190
00:09:14,900 --> 00:09:19,021
That's how you clean a glass stovetop
without scratching it.

191
00:09:19,382 --> 00:09:22,483
If your cooktop is shining again,
subscribe to

192
00:09:22,493 --> 00:09:27,101
WikiTube, because we publish a new how-to
every single day.

193
00:09:27,764 --> 00:09:29,704
Tell us in the comments what the worst

194
00:09:29,714 --> 00:09:31,875
spill on your stove has been, and what

195
00:09:31,885 --> 00:09:33,939
you would like us to explain next.

196
00:09:34,904 --> 00:09:36,134
See you tomorrow.

197
00:09:36,233 --> 00:09:37,370
That's WikiTube.

198
00:09:37,603 --> 00:09:39,727
Whatever it is, here's how.
